qcom-sensors-prebuilts (2.0.3-2~) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  [ Keerthi Gowda ]
  * debian/control: bump Standards-Version to 4.7.4, set Section to
      non-free/misc, drop Priority/Rules-Requires-Root, switch to
      Build-Depends-Arch for the arm64-specific dev dependencies, and
      add Homepage/Vcs-Browser/Vcs-Git
  * debian/rules: fix shebang and drop the no-op overrides for
      dh_auto_configure/dh_auto_build/dh_auto_clean/dh_install/
      dh_strip/dh_dwz/dh_shlibdeps/dh_fixperms, letting dh_shlibdeps run
      with default debhelper behaviour so the declared ${shlibs:Depends}
      reflect each package's actual runtime library dependencies
  * debian/control: add libglib2.0-dev to Build-Depends-Arch so
      dh_shlibdeps can resolve libglib-2.0.so.0 for qcom-sensors-test-apps,
      previously masked by the dh_shlibdeps no-op override
  * debian/watch: replace upstream.conf with a debian/watch file, matching
      pkg-btftm/pkg-ftm_ip convention; since the real prebuilt tarball
      (sensors-prebuilts.tar.gz) carries no version in its name, pin the
      Artifactory TAG in the URL and force the extracted version to the
      current upstream version via uversionmangle, to be bumped alongside
      the TAG on future releases
  * debian/rules: drop the data/ prefix from override_dh_auto_install's
      cp -a sources and remove the now-unused maintainerclean target;
      dpkg-source strips the orig tarball's sole top-level data/ directory
      on extraction (standard "3.0 (quilt)" behaviour for a single-directory
      tarball), so the installed packages must be copied from
      <package>/arm64/... directly, matching pkg-btftm/pkg-ftm_ip
  * debian/source/options: add extend-diff-ignore for .github and
      .gitignore
  * debian/gbp.conf: add gbp-buildpackage configuration
  * debian/source/lintian-overrides: add overrides for prebuilt-binary
      source package
  * .gitignore: add root .gitignore for build artifacts

 -- Keerthi Gowda <kbalehal@qti.qualcomm.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:30:00 +0000

